198 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
/E (Imagine an Indian train with many bogies connected together. Each bogie is a "Jodi" \(pair\) - it carries passengers AND connects to the next bogie. The whole train forms a "Silsila" \(chain\). You can easily add or remove bogies! But think of a bus - all seats are fixed in one place. You can't add more seats easily. That's the difference between linked lists and arrays!)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
